"""
Form-control geometry against Chrome 159 (headless shell 1255, Linux arm64,
`--force-device-scale-factor=1 --window-size=900,760`), where Chrome's control
font `13.3333px Arial` resolves to Liberation Sans and `monospace` to DejaVu
Sans Mono — the same faces this engine loads on Linux.

Every expected number below is a Chrome 159 `getBoundingClientRect()` value on
the fixture in that row; nothing is fitted to this engine's output.

FACE-DEPENDENT vs FACE-INDEPENDENT. Widths that come from glyph advances or
from the control face's average/maximum character width were measured on the
LINUX faces only. Those rows run when Liberation Sans and DejaVu Sans Mono are
the installed platform faces; on a Helvetica/Menlo host they are `pending`
(no Chrome 159 measurement exists for that face set here, and none is
invented), and on a host with neither they are BLOCKED. Everything that
follows from a UA rule instead of a face -- heights, borders, margins,
baseline placement, the 20 px select interior on an EMPTY select, which text a
control displays -- asserts on every host. The Helvetica/Menlo text-control
table is pinned separately, without loading a font, by the
`form_control_content_w_for_face` rows at the end and by
`form_control_intrinsic_width_spec`'s macOS column.

ROOTS this spec pins (each was red before its fix):

1. **A 5x7 bitmap-cell clamp leaked into real-face metrics.** The style stage
   clamped every resolved advance up to the inked width of the built-in bitmap
   glyph whenever `web_glyph_scale(font_size) == 1`. That is every size 8..15,
   not the `font_size <= 8` its comment promises, so at the 13 px control font
   Liberation Sans's `l` (3 px) became 4 and `Alpha` measured 34 instead of 33.
   `form_control_widget_box_spec` AC-12 went 73 -> 74 the day Linux
   `sans-serif` started resolving to Liberation Sans (whose `l` is narrower
   than the previous face's).

2. **`<select>` width is `ceil(widest label) + 20`, measured at the REAL
   control font size.** The old `SELECT_ARROW_WIDTH_PX = 22` was fitted on one
   label and silently absorbed two pixels of text under-measure (13 px instead
   of 13.3333 px, rounded instead of ceiled). Chrome's interior is exactly 20:
   an empty select is 20 + padding + border with or without author padding.

   | fixture                               | label px (Chrome span) | Chrome w |
   |---------------------------------------|------------------------|----------|
   | catalog CSS, `Alpha`/`Beta`           | 34.09                  | 73       |
   | catalog CSS, `A`                      |  8.89                  | 47       |
   | catalog CSS, `Alphabetical order`     | 107.44                 | 146      |
   | catalog CSS, `iiii`                   | 11.86                  | 50       |
   | catalog CSS, no option                |  0                     | 38       |
   | UA only, `Alpha`/`Beta`               | 34.09                  | 57       |
   | UA only, no option                    |  0                     | 22       |
   | UA only, `font-size:16px`, `Alpha`    | 40.92                  | 63       |

3. **`<select>` height carries 2 px of internal block padding**: 19 on a 15 px
   line with the UA's 1 px border, 35 with the catalog's `padding:8px`, 21 at
   16 px (17 px content area).

4. **Text-control width comes from the control FACE's metrics, not from one
   platform's fit.** Chrome's rule is `(size - 1) * round(avgCharWidth) +
   round(maxCharWidth)` for `<input>` and `cols * round(avgCharWidth) +
   scrollbar(15)` for `<textarea>`. For Liberation Sans at 13.3333 px that is
   `8N + 17` (xAvgCharWidth 1187/2048 em -> 7.73 -> 8; bbox 3780/2048 em ->
   24.6 -> 25) and for DejaVu Sans Mono `8N + 15`. The previous `7N + 5` /
   `8N + 17` were the Helvetica/Menlo numbers and stay in force on that host.

   | fixture                  | Chrome w |
   |--------------------------|----------|
   | UA `<input>` (size 20)   | 185      |
   | UA `<input size=10>`     | 105      |
   | UA `<input size=1>`      |  33      |
   | UA `<input size=40>`     | 345      |
   | catalog `<input>`        | 195      |
   | UA `<textarea>` (cols 20)| 181      |
   | UA `<textarea cols=10>`  | 101      |
   | UA `<textarea cols=40>`  | 341      |
   | catalog `<textarea>`     | 193      |

5. **A control's baseline is its INNER text baseline**, not a font strut hung
   from the top of its border box. Modelling it as the latter dropped every
   padded control 6 px below the top of its own line (input at y=14 in a label
   whose line starts at y=8; Chrome: 8).

6. **`<button>` width is its label at the real control font size** (Chrome
   119.48 for `Exercise controls`; this engine has integer boxes, so 120), and
   a button adds nothing to its line: the stale `+ 3` that outlived the removed
   UA margin made the last form line 36 where Chrome has 33.

7. **Checkbox and radio carry the UA margins** `3px 3px 3px 4px` and
   `3px 3px 0 5px`, so they start 4 / 5 px into their label.

8. **A control shows its own text.** The widget branch returns before child
   layout (a select's options are a popup, not flow), which also left a
   textarea's value and a select's current label with no box, so neither was
   painted: Chrome's `Editable text` and `Alpha` were blank boxes. The one
   text node each control displays is now laid out in its content box. These
   rows are the content-box arithmetic of the Chrome boxes above (text nodes
   inside a control are not reachable from script): border 1 + padding 8, plus
   the select's 1 px internal block padding, one 15 px line.

STATED RESIDUE (measured, not fixed here, see
doc/08_tracking/bug/web_form_control_chrome159_residue_2026-11-14.md):

- An author `font-size:13px` on a control is indistinguishable from the UA's
  13.3333 px (the cascade carries integer px), so that select is 57 against
  Chrome's 56.
- Checkbox/radio sit 1 px low (y=13 vs 12) and a textarea's label is 54 vs 55:
  both are the LINE strut baseline (18 here, 17 in Chrome, whose content area
  for Liberation Sans 16 px is 17 px, not 16), which belongs to inline text.
- `<input>` at author font sizes other than the UA's: Chrome's 16 px row (215)
  does not fit the rule above; only the UA size is pinned.
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-BROWSER-ENGINE-FORMS-003 — form-control boxes match Chrome 159 on the Linux system faces: select = ceil(label) + 20 wide and line + 2 tall, text controls size from the control face's average/maximum character width, controls align on their inner text baseline.
"""
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_engine.spl 1%
use std.spec.*
use std.nogc_sync_mut.sffi.io.{file_exists}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_foundation.{
    form_control_content_w_for_face
}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer.{
    simple_web_layout_debug_layout_by_id
}

val VW: i32 = 900
val VH: i32 = 760
val CAT: text = "<html><head><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;font:16px/1.5 sans-serif}label{display:block;margin:8px 0}input,select,textarea,button{padding:8px;border:1px solid #94a3b8}</style></head><body><form>"
val UA: text = "<html><head><style>body{margin:0;font:16px/1.5 sans-serif}</style></head><body><form>"

val LIB_SANS: text = "/usr/share/fonts/truetype/liberation/LiberationSans-Regular.ttf"
val DJV_MONO: text = "/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSansMono.ttf"
val HELVETICA_ID: text = "unmanaged=/System/Library/Fonts/Helvetica.ttc#0;bytes=0;axes=default"
val MENLO_ID: text = "unmanaged=/System/Library/Fonts/Menlo.ttc#0;bytes=0;axes=default"
val LIB_SANS_ID: text = "unmanaged=/usr/share/fonts/truetype/liberation/LiberationSans-Regular.ttf#0;bytes=410820;axes=default"
val DJV_MONO_ID: text = "unmanaged=/usr/share/fonts/truetype/dejavu/DejaVuSansMono.ttf#0;bytes=343140;axes=default"

fn macos_faces() -> bool:
    file_exists("/System/Library/Fonts/Helvetica.ttc")

fn linux_faces() -> bool:
    not macos_faces() and file_exists(LIB_SANS) and file_exists(DJV_MONO)

fn face_block_reason() -> text:
    if macos_faces():
        return "BLOCKED: no Chrome 159 measurement of this row on the Helvetica/Menlo face set; the numbers below are Liberation Sans / DejaVu Sans Mono"
    "BLOCKED: host has neither Helvetica/Menlo nor Liberation Sans / DejaVu Sans Mono under /usr/share/fonts"

fn cat(inner: text, prop: text) -> text:
    simple_web_layout_debug_layout_by_id(CAT + inner + "</form></body></html>", VW, VH, "x", prop)

fn ua(inner: text, prop: text) -> text:
    simple_web_layout_debug_layout_by_id(UA + inner + "</form></body></html>", VW, VH, "x", prop)

describe "select width is ceil(widest label) + 20 at the real control font":
    it "sizes the catalog select from its widest option":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        step("Alpha is 34.09 px at 13.3333 px: 35 + 20 + 16 + 2")
        expect(cat("<select id=\"x\"><option>Alpha</option><option>Beta</option></select>", "w")).to_equal("73")

    it "sizes a one-glyph label":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        step("A is 8.89 px: 9 + 20 + 18")
        expect(cat("<select id=\"x\"><option>A</option></select>", "w")).to_equal("47")

    it "sizes a long label without drifting":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        step("107.44 px: 108 + 20 + 18 — a fitted constant is off by one here")
        expect(cat("<select id=\"x\"><option>Alphabetical order</option></select>", "w")).to_equal("146")

    it "sizes a label made only of narrow glyphs":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        step("iiii is 11.86 px; the bitmap-cell clamp made each i a pixel wider")
        expect(cat("<select id=\"x\"><option>iiii</option></select>", "w")).to_equal("50")

    it "gives an empty select exactly the 20 px interior":
        expect(cat("<select id=\"x\"></select>", "w")).to_equal("38")

    it "keeps the same interior with only the UA border":
        expect(ua("<select id=\"x\"></select>", "w")).to_equal("22")

    it "adds the label to that interior with only the UA border":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        expect(ua("<select id=\"x\"><option>Alpha</option><option>Beta</option></select>", "w")).to_equal("57")

    it "follows an author font size on the select":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        step("Alpha is 40.92 px at 16 px: 41 + 20 + 2")
        expect(ua("<select id=\"x\" style=\"font-size:16px\"><option>Alpha</option></select>", "w")).to_equal("63")

describe "select height is its line plus 2 px of internal padding":
    it "is 35 with the catalog padding":
        expect(cat("<select id=\"x\"><option>Alpha</option><option>Beta</option></select>", "h")).to_equal("35")

    it "is 19 with only the UA border":
        expect(ua("<select id=\"x\"><option>Alpha</option><option>Beta</option></select>", "h")).to_equal("19")

    it "grows its label to 35":
        expect(cat("<label id=\"x\">Choice <select><option>Alpha</option><option>Beta</option></select></label>", "h")).to_equal("35")

describe "text controls size from the control face's metrics":
    it "gives the UA <input> its 20 columns":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        step("19 x 8 + 25 content, 4 padding, 4 border")
        expect(ua("<input id=\"x\">", "w")).to_equal("185")

    it "makes the UA <input> 21 tall: one 15 px line, 1 px padding, 2 px border":
        expect(ua("<input id=\"x\">", "h")).to_equal("21")

    it "scales with the size attribute":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        expect(ua("<input id=\"x\" size=\"10\">", "w")).to_equal("105")
        expect(ua("<input id=\"x\" size=\"1\">", "w")).to_equal("33")
        expect(ua("<input id=\"x\" size=\"40\">", "w")).to_equal("345")

    it "gives the catalog <input> Chrome's 195":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        expect(cat("<label>Name <input id=\"x\" value=\"Simple\"></label>", "w")).to_equal("195")

    it "gives the UA <textarea> its 20 columns and scrollbar gutter":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        step("20 x 8 + 15 content, 4 padding, 2 border; two 15 px rows")
        expect(ua("<textarea id=\"x\"></textarea>", "w")).to_equal("181")

    it "makes the UA <textarea> 36 tall: two 15 px rows, 2 px padding, 1 px border":
        expect(ua("<textarea id=\"x\"></textarea>", "h")).to_equal("36")

    it "scales with the cols attribute":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        expect(ua("<textarea id=\"x\" cols=\"10\"></textarea>", "w")).to_equal("101")
        expect(ua("<textarea id=\"x\" cols=\"40\"></textarea>", "w")).to_equal("341")

    it "gives the catalog <textarea> Chrome's 193":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        expect(cat("<label>Notes <textarea id=\"x\">Editable text</textarea></label>", "w")).to_equal("193")

describe "a control aligns on its inner text baseline":
    it "puts a padded <input> at the top of its label line":
        step("was 14: the control hung from a 13 px font strut, 6 px low")
        expect(cat("<label>Name <input id=\"x\" value=\"Simple\"></label>", "y")).to_equal("8")
        expect(cat("<label id=\"x\">Name <input value=\"Simple\"></label>", "h")).to_equal("33")

    it "puts a padded <select> at the top of its label line":
        expect(cat("<label>Choice <select id=\"x\"><option>Alpha</option><option>Beta</option></select></label>", "y")).to_equal("8")

    it "puts a <textarea> at the top of its label line":
        expect(cat("<label>Notes <textarea id=\"x\">Editable text</textarea></label>", "y")).to_equal("8")

describe "button box":
    it "is as wide as its label at the control font size":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        step("Chrome 119.48: label 101.48 + 16 + 2; integer boxes ceil the label")
        expect(cat("<button id=\"x\" type=\"button\">Exercise controls</button>", "w")).to_equal("120")

    it "is 33 tall with the catalog padding":
        expect(cat("<button id=\"x\" type=\"button\">Exercise controls</button>", "h")).to_equal("33")

    it "is the same width as a flex item":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        step("the real-size label rule lives in both intrinsic walkers, not one call site")
        expect(cat("<div style=\"display:flex\"><button id=\"x\" type=\"button\">Exercise controls</button></div>", "w")).to_equal("120")

    it "keeps its label on one line inside that box":
        expect(cat("<button id=\"x\" type=\"button\">Exercise controls</button>", "text_h")).to_equal("15")

    it "adds nothing to the height of its line":
        step("was 36: a stale + 3 from a UA margin that no longer exists")
        expect(cat("<button type=\"button\">Exercise controls</button><output>Not exercised</output><div id=\"x\">after</div>", "y")).to_equal("33")

describe "checkbox and radio UA margins":
    it "starts a checkbox 4 px into its label":
        expect(cat("<label><input id=\"x\" type=\"checkbox\" checked> Enabled</label>", "x")).to_equal("4")

    it "starts a radio 5 px into its label":
        expect(cat("<label><input id=\"x\" type=\"radio\" checked> Light</label>", "x")).to_equal("5")

    it "keeps each control's own UA margins when several inputs share a parent":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        step("the cascade memo keyed on the tag alone handed the checkbox the text input's style")
        expect(cat("<input value=\"a\"><input id=\"x\" type=\"checkbox\"><input type=\"radio\">", "x")).to_equal("199")
        expect(cat("<input value=\"a\"><input type=\"checkbox\"><input id=\"x\" type=\"radio\">", "x")).to_equal("220")

    it "keeps each control's own margins when several inputs share a parent, on any face":
        step("margin-top is 3 px on the checkbox, 0 on the text input beside it; margin-bottom 0 on the radio")
        expect(cat("<input value=\"a\"><input id=\"x\" type=\"checkbox\"><input type=\"radio\">", "margin_t")).to_equal("3")
        expect(cat("<input id=\"x\" value=\"a\"><input type=\"checkbox\"><input type=\"radio\">", "margin_t")).to_equal("0")
        expect(cat("<input value=\"a\"><input type=\"checkbox\"><input id=\"x\" type=\"radio\">", "margin_b")).to_equal("0")
        expect(cat("<input value=\"a\"><input id=\"x\" type=\"checkbox\"><input type=\"radio\">", "margin_b")).to_equal("3")

    it "keeps both at 13x13 and their label at one 24 px line":
        expect(cat("<label><input id=\"x\" type=\"checkbox\" checked> Enabled</label>", "w")).to_equal("13")
        expect(cat("<label><input id=\"x\" type=\"radio\" checked> Light</label>", "h")).to_equal("13")
        expect(cat("<label id=\"x\"><input type=\"checkbox\" checked> Enabled</label>", "h")).to_equal("24")

describe "a control lays out the one text it displays":
    it "gives a textarea's value a line at its content-box top":
        step("label line at y=8; border 1 + padding 8")
        expect(cat("<label>Notes <textarea id=\"x\">Editable text</textarea></label>", "text_y")).to_equal("17")
        expect(cat("<label>Notes <textarea id=\"x\">Editable text</textarea></label>", "text_h")).to_equal("15")

    it "gives a select's first option label a line inside the select":
        step("border 1 + padding 8 + the menulist's 1 px block padding")
        expect(cat("<label>Choice <select><option id=\"x\">Alpha</option><option>Beta</option></select></label>", "text_y")).to_equal("18")
        expect(cat("<label>Choice <select><option id=\"x\">Alpha</option><option>Beta</option></select></label>", "text_h")).to_equal("15")

    it "shows the selected option, not the first":
        expect(cat("<select><option>Alpha</option><option id=\"x\" selected>Beta</option></select>", "text_h")).to_equal("15")
        expect(cat("<select><option id=\"x\">Alpha</option><option selected>Beta</option></select>", "text_h")).to_equal("0")

    it "keeps a select's label on one line however narrow the select":
        step("a 60 px select is still 35 tall in Chrome; the label must not wrap under it")
        expect(cat("<select id=\"x\" style=\"width:60px\"><option>Alphabetical order</option></select>", "h")).to_equal("35")
        expect(cat("<select style=\"width:60px\"><option id=\"x\">Alphabetical order</option></select>", "text_h")).to_equal("15")

    it "still gives no option an in-flow box":
        expect(cat("<select><option id=\"x\">Alpha</option><option>Beta</option></select>", "h")).to_equal("0")
        expect(cat("<select><option id=\"x\">Alpha</option><option>Beta</option></select>", "w")).to_equal("0")

    it "keeps the select's own width when its label gets a box":
        if not linux_faces():
            pending(face_block_reason())
            return
        expect(cat("<select id=\"x\"><option>Alpha</option><option>Beta</option></select>", "w")).to_equal("73")

describe "the text-control width table is keyed by face, and the macOS faces keep theirs":
    it "gives Helvetica the original 7N + 5 input content width":
        step("163 / 93 / 58 on the catalog page are these plus 18 px of padding and border")
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("input", HELVETICA_ID, 20, 1)).to_equal(145)
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("input", HELVETICA_ID, 10, 1)).to_equal(75)
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("input", HELVETICA_ID, 5, 1)).to_equal(40)

    it "gives Menlo the original 8N + 17 textarea content width":
        step("195 / 115 / 355 on the catalog page")
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("textarea", MENLO_ID, 20, 1)).to_equal(177)
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("textarea", MENLO_ID, 10, 1)).to_equal(97)
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("textarea", MENLO_ID, 40, 1)).to_equal(337)

    it "gives Liberation Sans 8N + 17 and DejaVu Sans Mono 8N + 15":
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("input", LIB_SANS_ID, 20, 1)).to_equal(177)
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("input", LIB_SANS_ID, 1, 1)).to_equal(25)
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("textarea", DJV_MONO_ID, 20, 1)).to_equal(175)
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("textarea", DJV_MONO_ID, 40, 1)).to_equal(335)

    it "keeps the original table for any face it does not know":
        step("an unresolved face must not silently take the Linux numbers")
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("input", "", 20, 1)).to_equal(145)
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("textarea", "", 20, 1)).to_equal(177)
        expect(form_control_content_w_for_face("textarea", LIB_SANS_ID, 20, 1)).to_equal(177)
